  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authority & staleness",
      "items": [
        "DESCRIPTIVE / NON-AUTHORITATIVE. Observes MQD; does not control it.",
        "STALE IF VIEWED AGAINST A DIFFERENT REPOSITORY COMMIT. Anchor: c81695de (full 40-char SHA in every SRC link, the README and the provenance file).",
        "Authority order: code/tests/Git/DB proof, then binding specs and ledgers, then this diagram.",
        "SRC badges are verified against committed blobs at the anchor. Edges carry no individual source references; see the README evidence table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Authority boundaries",
      "items": [
        "RESEARCH HAS NO ORDER-SUBMISSION AUTHORITY: research-py and mqk-backtest have no broker or outbox path.",
        "Research reaches runtime only via the Promotion Gate: operator POST, evidence re-validated, durable transition row.",
        "Strategy-originated orders need an exact (strategy_id, symbol, timeframe) active_paper row bound to the strategy config fingerprint; registered + enabled is never tradable. The manual operator order route is a separate admission surface outside this gate.",
        "Promotion gate hard-codes tradable_live = false and denies Live and Unknown modes (including LiveShadow) for strategy-originated orders."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Paper vs Live",
      "items": [
        "Paper + Alpaca (paper-api.alpaca.markets) is the intended promotion-gated order-submitting runtime mode.",
        "LiveShadow is wired for real Alpaca connectivity (api.alpaca.markets). Do NOT read it as monitor-only or no-order: its daemon-wide no-order truth is NOT PROVEN at this anchor (see the LiveShadow gap card).",
        "LiveCapital order execution is not enabled: start is refused unless live_trust_complete=true, which the current parity pipeline cannot produce.",
        "Broker connectivity is not order authority. Documented state at the anchor, NOT runtime-verified: Paper INACTIVE, Live DISABLED (documentation wording), no promoted candidate, PROMOTION_AUTHORITY = NONE."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "LiveShadow order-authority gap",
      "items": [
        "Canonical LiveShadow launcher: real Alpaca connectivity, but the launcher does not arm, start the execution runtime, or submit orders.",
        "Strategy-originated LiveShadow decisions fail closed before the outbox: LiveShadow maps to PromotionRunMode::Live, which the promotion gate denies (internal decision seam and strategy signal route; DB-backed test cited in the README).",
        "SAFETY DISCREPANCY: the generic arm and run-start routes have no deployment-mode fence, and POST /api/v1/execution/orders is a separate order-admission route outside the promotion gate. An existing hermetic proof (cited in the README) creates a PENDING manual-order outbox row under LiveShadow.",
        "Therefore daemon-wide LiveShadow no-order truth is NOT PROVEN at this anchor. Whether such a row can reach a broker is a separate, untested safety question. Actual live-broker submission was NOT tested and is NOT claimed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Broker truth",
      "items": [
        "Broker events are the only source of acks and fills: events → oms_inbox (deduplicated) → OMS/portfolio apply.",
        "MQD does not synthesize fills, acknowledgements or cancel confirmations.",
        "Reconcile compares local OMS/portfolio state to an external REST broker snapshot (Alpaca); the local LockedPaperBroker is refused as an execution path.",
        "Account-level risk reads the same broker snapshot as its authority."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Durable vs transient",
      "items": [
        "Durable (Postgres): runs, outbox, inbox, arm state, promotion transitions, md_bars, audit_events, held-sizing state.",
        "Transient (process memory): IntegrityState, reconcile status, broker snapshot cache, pending bar input, risk state.",
        "After restart the DB is authoritative; OMS and portfolio are recovered from it (restart recovery in daemon snapshot code)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Not shown, conceptual or unknown",
      "items": [
        "CONCEPTUAL / NOT ENABLED: LiveCapital order execution (start refused), non-equity asset classes (V2 scaffold), IBKR adapter (not a daemon dependency).",
        "UNKNOWN: whether a daemon is running, Paper DB contents and migration level, deployed strategy; whether a LiveShadow PENDING manual-order row can reach a broker (untested).",
        "INFERRED: 'research has no order path' is a repository-search result, not a proof; research-py's only network egress found is GET to data.alpaca.markets.",
        "Not drawn: CLI direct DB bookkeeping (mqk run/db/ingest), WS transport and gap recovery, Postgres audit_events, crypto and option modules."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Where the code and its docs disagree",
      "items": [
        "The completed-bar driver module header says it is not started from main.rs; main.rs spawns it for Paper+Alpaca.",
        "mqk-daemon declares mqk-audit but never uses it; audit rows go to Postgres audit_events via mqk-db.",
        "README_TECHNICAL.md cites an older accepted baseline than this anchor.",
        "SAFETY DISCREPANCY: LiveShadow is documented as no-order, but the manual order route and generic arm/start are not mode-fenced; see the LiveShadow gap card. Observational only, not repaired here."
